{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-73","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：可公度量与截差无理线段与无理线段","englishTitle":"If from a rational straight line there be subtracted a rational straight line commensurable with the whole in square only, the remainder is irrational; and let it be called an apotome.","book":10,"number":73,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.73","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.73/","group":"prop_2","sourceNumber":73,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","contentId":"euclid-10-73","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"814aca45d19fea9d93b46d4b54742971754cad99ec7eb47a0f1dcc9eb4d7f096","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-73.statement","euclid-10-73.proof.1","euclid-10-73.proof.2","euclid-10-73.proof.3","euclid-10-73.proof.4","euclid-10-73.proof.5","euclid-10-73.conclusion","euclid-10-73.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-73.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"44b540052175beb457020b765c20ede97578a7c4713eaa425aa8b360c31a3ff9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If from a rational straight line there be subtracted a rational straight line commensurable with the whole in square only, the remainder is irrational; and let it be called an apotome."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果从有理线段减去有理线段 可公度,而整个仅以正方形计,则其余为无理;让它称为截差无理线段。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-73.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":1,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7988211ece525f18236d0d0eef30399abe79f0e9d0f4cc9199eed7bf74239635","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For from the rational straight line AB let the rational straight line BC, commensurable with the whole in square only, be subtracted; I say that the remainder AC is the irrational straight line called apotome."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"从有理线段 AB中减去有理线段 BC,可公度中仅用正方形,其余的AC是无理线段,称为截差无理线段。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-73.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c0c4b2dace9c9e83c1daa600ae3a6fd1cabfc2873b4fb6d6b797b508b48c7fbe","citations":["euclid-10-11"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since AB is incommensurable in length with BC, and, as AB is to BC, so is the square on AB to the rectangle AB, BC, therefore the square on AB is incommensurable with the rectangle AB, BC. [[X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为AB的长度是不可公度,BC,AB与BC的比等于正方形的AB与矩形的BC和BC的BC的比,因此,AB的正方形与矩形的AB和BC的BC的比是不可公度 [[X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-73.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e801e9343da89f25dcce13e5e673a8eab887479509f611473dda872cb7ebdd4d","citations":["euclid-10-15","euclid-10-6"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the squares on AB, BC are commensurable with the square on AB, [[X. 15](/principles/euclid-10-15)] and twice the rectangle AB, BC is commensurable with the rectangle AB, BC. [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AB的正方形,BC是可公度,AB是正方形,矩形是AB的两倍,矩形,BC是可公度,矩形是BC。 [[X. 15](/principles/euclid-10-15)] [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-73.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b700eaeff8cacb3906e9360e4ccdf0536350118ff4843d9b19babec7dddfcaac","citations":["euclid-2-7","euclid-10-13"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, inasmuch as the squares on AB, BC are equal to twice the rectangle AB, BC together with the square on CA, [[II. 7](/principles/euclid-2-7)] therefore the squares on AB, BC are also incommensurable with the remainder, the square on AC. [[X. 13, 16](/principles/euclid-10-13)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"AB的正方形,BC是矩形的两倍,BC是矩形的两倍,CA是正方形,CA是AB,BC也是不可公度,其余的正方形是AC。 [[II. 7](/principles/euclid-2-7)] [[X. 13, 16](/principles/euclid-10-13)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-73.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ef495e0e02f9b49cd7ed4026b36d0b9b3b52dcb860a55d157bc61d6bceca1bb1","citations":["euclid-10-def-4"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the squares on AB, BC are rational; therefore AC is irrational. [[X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AB,BC的正方形是有理,因此AC是无理。 [[X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-73.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":6,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"cfa36dafe00c555ee3c7c7f576d8f4ab4d510c45aa4e911fffa8ca1e11a80362","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And let it be called an apotome. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让它被称为截差无理线段。证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-73.source","contentId":"euclid-10-73","revisionId":"euclid-10-73@raw-814aca45d19fea9d","order":7,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"256d0a03b4d1209ba126e11e9f098638b9d1cd990f493fac79b86dd2fb1917a1","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.73/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.73\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-73:euclid-10-11:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-73","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-73.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-11","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.73","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.73/","sourceLabel":"X. 11"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-10-73:euclid-10-15:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-73","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-73.proof.3"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-15","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","ba